omes of each lottery independent of their probabilities and dividing by the number of outcomes'. The key is 'number of outcomes' — if 'outcomes' means distinct possible results, A has three: 4000, 2000, 0; B has two: 6000, 0. So mean A: 2000, B: 3000 → prefers B. But if 'outcomes' means all possible result values listed once regardless of probability, same result. So the reason can be applied, and it prefers B.",
